p(20,9,"Only ignorance! only ignorance! how can you talk about only",
 "John says that ignorance is the worst thing in the world next to wickedness. People who say \"I did not know\" can still do great harm, and he gives the example of Martha Mulwash.",
 "John says: “Only ignorance! How can you talk about only ignorance? Don’t you know that it is the worst thing in the world, after wickedness? And only heaven knows which does the most harm. If people can say, ‘Oh, I did not know, I did not mean any harm,’ they think it is all right. I think Martha Mulwash did not mean to kill that baby when she gave it Dalby and soothing syrups. But she did kill it, and she was tried for killing someone without meaning to.”",
 ["ignorance","wickedness","mischief","dosed","soothing syrups","manslaughter"])
s(20,"Don’t you know that it is the worst thing in the world",
 "You know that it is the worst thing in the world, after wickedness, do you not?",
 "A negative question, 'Don’t you know...?', is used to say strongly that the person does know; 'next to' here means 'after'.")
